<title>POLAND: Polish zloty fixed weaker at 3.12 pct from parity.</title>
<headline>Polish zloty fixed weaker at 3.12 pct from parity.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.0235 to the dollar, down from 3.0110 yesterday and at 1.7965 to the mark, up from 1.8000, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 3.12 percent from the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, weaker from Tuesday's fix at 3.21 percent.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
